{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CgeZ9U6rHpdEMR6Qbrygh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n    \"name\": \"Instructor for PHP\",\n    \"targetAudience\": \"P&C Insurance CIOs and Enterprise Technology Leaders\",\n    \"technologies\": [\n        \"PHP\",\n        \"LLM APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Ollama)\",\n        \"Polyglot Inference Engine\",\n        \"Vector Databases (Qdrant, Pgvector)\",\n        \"Laravel and Symfony Frameworks\",\n        \"JSON Schema\",\n        \"Symfony Validation\"\n    ],\n    \"features\": [\n        \"Structured data extraction from unstructured insurance documents and claims\",\n        \"Validation and automated data quality enforcement\",\n        \"Multi-provider LLM abstraction for vendor flexibility and cost optimization\",\n        \"Batch inference for high-volume claims processing\",\n        \"Vector embeddings and semantic search for document retrieval\",\n        \"Agentic AI for autonomous claims assessment and policy analysis\",\n        \"RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) for contextual insurance decision-making\",\n        \"Framework-native integration with Laravel and Symfony\",\n        \"Observability and audit trails via events and structured logging\"\n    ],\n    \"applications\": [\n        \"Automated claims document parsing and classification (OCR/image extraction)\",\n        \"Policy holder information extraction and entity resolution\",\n        \"Risk assessment and underwriting automation\",\n        \"Fraud detection through semantic analysis of claim patterns\",\n        \"Coverage eligibility determination from policy documents\",\n        \"Loss reserve estimation and reserve adequacy analysis\",\n        \"Customer inquiry handling via AI agents with tool-using capabilities\",\n        \"Regulatory compliance documentation and evidence assembly\",\n        \"Legacy system data migration and normalization\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Instructor for PHP solves the critical enterprise challenge of integrating Large Language Models into P&C insurance operations without vendor lock-in or architectural debt. Insurance CIOs face mounting pressure to reduce manual claims processing, improve underwriting velocity, and extract value from unstructured data—policy documents, claim forms, medical reports, and correspondence. Instructor provides an enterprise-grade abstraction layer that decouples your systems from any single LLM provider, enabling you to develop once and deploy across OpenAI, Anthropic, or cost-effective alternatives like Groq or Ollama. Its validation framework ensures extracted insurance data meets regulatory standards and business rules automatically. The batch inference capability handles thousands of claims asynchronously, while the built-in RAG and vector storage enable claims analysts to retrieve relevant precedent and policy language instantly. With native Laravel and Symfony integration, it fits seamlessly into existing PHP infrastructure.\",\n    \"code\": \"```php\\nuse Cognesy\\\\Instructor\\\\StructuredOutput;\\nuse Symfony\\\\Component\\\\Validator\\\\Constraints as Assert;\\n\\n// Define structured claim data model\\nclass ClaimExtraction {\\n    #[Assert\\\\NotBlank]\\n    public string $claimNumber;\\n    \\n    #[Assert\\\\Choice(choices: ['auto', 'property', 'workers_comp', 'liability'])]\\n    public string $lossType;\\n    \\n    #[Assert\\\\Range(min: 0)]\\n    public float $estimatedLosses;\\n    \\n    public string $description;\\n}\\n\\n// Extract structured data from unstructured claim document\\n$claimText = file_get_contents('claim_form.pdf'); // or image\\n\\n$extracted = (new StructuredOutput)\\n    ->withResponseClass(ClaimExtraction::class)\\n    ->with(messages: $claimText)\\n    ->withOptions(['max_tokens' => 1000])\\n    ->get(); // Validates automatically, retries on failure\\n\\n// Type-safe access to extracted claim data\\necho \\\"Claim {$extracted->claimNumber}: {$extracted->lossType} - \\\\${$extracted->estimatedLosses}\\\";\\n\\n// Switch providers without code changes\\n$extracted = (new StructuredOutput)\\n    ->usingProvider('anthropic') // Was 'openai', now using Claude\\n    ->withResponseClass(ClaimExtraction::class)\\n    ->with(messages: $claimText)\\n    ->get();\\n```\"\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":471,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6271,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6271,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":985,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}